 "text": "Hello there! How's your day? It can be strange to some people. Some cemeteries ban it. Many do, especially in the spring. The dead come spring cleaning, and cleaning table is taken very literally. Bring little food, always bring sweets, and always ask first. Some cemeteries even supply a spot for it. Some cemeteries ban it altogether, so it' best not to take any risk. The big threat is a quiet little alert about a coin hitting the ground. A friendly hello to the museum or office usually gets you through.",
